From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] wifi: mt76: mt7615: drive a part whose firmware owns the MAC

On a part whose firmware owns the MAC:

  - skip MAC and PHY register access, each an unanswered mailbox round
    trip
  - skip the commands it lacks: DBDC, MAC enable, channel switch, rx
    path, SKU, protection, RTS, ARP and GTK rekey offload, and the rate
    power table. Each costs a full MCU timeout; GTK rekey offload alone
    held every reconnect for 20 s
  - join with CH_PRIVILEGE, BSS activation and a station record, and on
    leave drop every station of the BSS, or later scans never complete
  - raise the BSS before a scan, since the firmware probes from it, and
    scan one band per request, the most a version 0 request lists
  - send keys by command, rejecting unsupported ciphers before any state
    changes
  - leave transmit block ack to the firmware, and follow its receive
    session events with mac80211's offloaded sessions
  - transmit data as 802.3 with the firmware building the header, strip
    the header each frame actually carries on completion, and leave
    receive header translation off, which mac80211 takes only after the
    handshake
  - use the BSS as the own-MAC index, the first WMM set, and table
    entries above the ones the firmware keeps
  - advertise station mode only, without 160 MHz

System suspend is untested and still sends the MT7663's HIF suspend
commands.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
